Everything in packaging/ that is ours - the templates `cargo xtask package`
turns into the unsigned zips' README.txt and REUSE.toml, and this directory's
README.md - is licensed under either of

  * MIT License            (../LICENSES/MIT.txt)
  * Apache License, 2.0    (../LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

at your option, like the documentation.

Two files in this directory are quoted verbatim from elsewhere and keep their
own terms: LICENSE-MPL-2.0.txt is the Mozilla Public License 2.0 and
LICENSE-BSL-1.0.txt the Boost Software License 1.0, the canonical texts from
the SPDX licence list. They are here because crates compiled into the shipped
binaries are under those licences (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt in each zip names
them), and each zip's LICENSES/ carries them. This repository's own code uses
neither, which is why they are not in ../LICENSES/.

The repository-wide scheme is described in ../LICENSE and in
../docs/LICENSING.md; the machine-readable manifest is ../REUSE.toml.
